# Cloudflare Workers static-assets headers (_headers).
#
# Serve the Markdown docs endpoints as UTF-8 markdown. Cloudflare's default
# `.md` asset content-type is `text/markdown` WITHOUT a charset, so browsers
# fall back to windows-1252 and mojibake Vietnamese (/vi/*.md) pages. This rule
# pins the charset for every `.md` asset — both the new sibling `/{lang}/{page}.md`
# endpoints and the existing `/{lang}/llms.mdx/docs/.../content.md` files.
#
# NOTE: the trailing-literal glob (`/*.md`) must be verified against the live
# Workers static-assets matcher on staging; keep this scoped to `.md` only so it
# never overrides the content-type of HTML pages.
#
# X-Robots-Tag: noindex keeps these out of the search index as duplicates of
# their HTML page (which carries the real canonical/indexing signal) while
# leaving them crawlable — robots.txt does NOT block them (issue #61), since
# a crawl block would hide this header/the AI-crawler-facing Markdown mirror
# (issue #29) from crawlers entirely instead of just keeping it unindexed.
/*.md
  Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
